00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:04.036
And while we knew helping you modernize faster would be Popular,

00:40:04.676 --> 00:40:13.956
it turns out that there's a really long list of legacy code
that you want to transform things like Python, JavaScript,

00:40:14.316 --> 00:40:17.836
C2, Roche, migrations, and many, many more.

00:40:18.316 --> 00:40:23.196
So we ask ourselves, why not support all modernizations?

00:40:23.516 --> 00:40:26.876
And that's why we built AWS Transform custom.

00:40:27.396 --> 00:40:35.716
Now you can create transformation agents
that can modernize any code, API, runtime,

00:40:35.996 --> 00:40:41.676
even programming languages and frameworks
that are unique to your company.

00:40:42.036 --> 00:40:47.196
It continuously improves accuracy by
learning from every execution and code change,

00:40:47.476 --> 00:40:51.756
making each transformation more reliable and efficient.

00:40:52.076 --> 00:41:00.836
With transform, you can finally tackle those migration
projects and get back to building features that truly matter.

00:41:01.716 --> 00:41:08.556
Which is exactly what Air Canada
did with thousands of Lambda functions running

00:41:08.596 --> 00:41:17.036
on Node.js. 16 Air Canada needed
to modernize to the more capable Node.js training.

00:41:17.396 --> 00:41:26.596
The team was able to deploy AWS Transform to coordinate and execute
their modernization in just a few days with transform.

00:41:26.636 --> 00:41:36.556
They saw an 80% reduction in both time and cost compared to what
they had originally expected for their modernization project.

00:41:36.956 --> 00:41:43.756
We are thrilled to see what agents are delivering value for you. Now,

00:41:44.436 --> 00:41:54.316
I am truly honored and pleased to welcome the president and Group CEO
of Certis, Ng Tian Beng to share how they are bringing agents

00:41:54.316 --> 00:42:01.236
and robotics together on AWS to reimagine security operations.

00:42:01.596 --> 00:42:02.196
Welcome.

00:42:30.996 --> 00:42:34.636
Thank you Jaime. Good morning, ladies and gentlemen.

00:42:35.076 --> 00:42:38.916
I'm very pleased to be here.
And it looks like I'm joined by a colleague.

00:42:41.356 --> 00:42:43.996
MAX, could you please say hello to our guests?

00:42:47.276 --> 00:42:52.156
Hello, everyone. It is a pleasure
to be here at the AWS Summit, Singapore.

00:42:52.636 --> 00:42:55.956
Welcome, and I hope you enjoy today's keynote.

00:42:57.156 --> 00:42:57.996
Thank you MAX.

00:43:03.396 --> 00:43:06.076
Let me introduce Max to all of you.

00:43:06.956 --> 00:43:10.716
MAX stands for Multi-Service Autonomous Executive.

00:43:11.076 --> 00:43:16.356
He's a humanoid concierge,
and he's an example of a new generation of robotics.

00:43:16.636 --> 00:43:19.116
We are bringing into real world operations.

00:43:20.116 --> 00:43:24.596
I know it looks simple, but it
represents something much, much bigger for us.

00:43:24.956 --> 00:43:32.356
It's a future that we are building at Certis,
where AI and robotics are embedded into real life operations.

00:43:33.156 --> 00:43:42.436
It's a world where intelligent systems can serve as AI agents
to communicate, to understand context and work alongside humans.

00:43:43.076 --> 00:43:46.076
This is a direction that Certis is going.

00:43:47.636 --> 00:43:49.556
Let me briefly talk about our history.

00:43:49.836 --> 00:43:55.676
We began in 1958 as a guard and escort
unit within the Singapore Police Force.

00:43:56.036 --> 00:44:01.276
In 2005 we corporatized and became a Temasek portfolio company.

00:44:01.916 --> 00:44:05.636
We have now more than 60 years of being part of Singapore's history.

00:44:06.036 --> 00:44:13.036
We secure aviation sites like Changi Airport,
critical infrastructure, commercial estates and more.

00:44:14.996 --> 00:44:18.956
Today, we employ more than 25,000 people across the world.

00:44:19.556 --> 00:44:22.636
Half of them are here in Singapore and on the front lines.

00:44:24.476 --> 00:44:29.756
However, like many other manpower intensive industries,
we do have a fundamental challenge.

00:44:30.236 --> 00:44:37.676
While the demand for our services is growing quickly,
the supply of manpower willing to do frontline jobs is very tight.

00:44:38.236 --> 00:44:41.356
So in 2018, we actually made a decision.

00:44:42.116 --> 00:44:47.516
Instead of asking how technology can support
our operations, we asked a bigger question.

00:44:47.836 --> 00:44:55.996
We ask how should operations themselves be redesigned for worldwide,
AI and automation are becoming part of the workforce.

00:44:57.876 --> 00:45:00.000
Two technologies sit at the center of this modernization.

